Hello!

I booted my laptop normally, then some hours later ran 'systemctl 
hibernate'. The next day when I powered it on it resumed as it was 
supposed to, but the wifi was down. dmesg showed lots of "[ cut here ]" 
about the mt7601u module (see attached file). For some reason I had the 
bright idea to try and reload the module (without unplugging the 
dongle). 'modprobe -r mt7601u' completed after a few seconds, but then 
'modprobe mt7601u' just turned on the Caps Lock LED and froze the 
system. I killed it by pressing and holding the power button.

The dongle is a Tenda W311MI 150 Mbps. lsusb says:

Bus 002 Device 002: ID 148f:7601 Ralink Technology, Corp. MT7601U 
Wireless Adapter

The router is a cheap b/g Belkin configured for WPA2 "personal".

The laptop is an HP Compaq 6720s.

I'm using connman 1.35 with wpa_supplicant 2.6. The kernel is 4.9.77 
from the Arch Linux package "linux-lts" 4.9.77-1. I updated Arch Linux 
five days ago (January 19).

I'm attaching the output from journalctl starting at the boot just 
before I hibernated the system, up to the point where I killed it with 
the power button.

Maybe it's unrelated, but maybe it's just unhelpful: out of about six 
attempts to hibernate this laptop, at least three resulted in a locked 
up system after resuming from hibernation. It gets as far as showing my 
desktop as I left it, and then it immediately gets stuck that way. The 
Caps Lock LED doesn't light up. I can only kill it by holding the power 
button, and there is nothing in journalctl.

Initially I was running the 4.14.13 kernel (Arch Linux package "linux" 
4.14.13-1), but the system kept locking up after resuming, as described 
in the previous paragraph. This is why I tried the 4.9.77 kernel, with 
the same result, except for the one time so far where the wifi was dead 
but the rest of the system worked.

The wifi dongle was plugged in during all attempts to hibernate. I 
haven't unplugged it yet since buying it.

